{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788416054443269001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"witted-invisible-roan","assignee":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":5,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"6662ce541e663f1ffcc07e09d249c878cd2a454723d9fd60bfabd7bc54efb899","event_uuid":"97efd87a-2d6b-4333-a55e-5833d9d07cce","position":{"commit_sha":"b1505c02d6d344197b24040d1681797e681b2330","position":"1788411304995986001-97efd87a-2d6b-4333-a55e-5833d9d07cce"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"02c6958865d8284593889fec3fc79cdd84b4b14c416c410cad20732553405e1c","event_uuid":"6a7ad30c-7ec9-44b6-9fd0-f9d3a3c457af","position":{"commit_sha":"7fc419dcbfde4b270e8d20d31fc7f7929f235c9e","position":"1788411323175569001-6a7ad30c-7ec9-44b6-9fd0-f9d3a3c457af"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6989bce6e3c6024e51ab8ea8f50abb2d45b4908c292ad7c97c533c593a8f1481","event_uuid":"9f9a407a-1e5d-4fcf-8665-e5566c16db9d","position":{"commit_sha":"6ac0a05d369cedbfbedf1f75fc9f742ebc8e9c45","position":"1788411451129139001-9f9a407a-1e5d-4fcf-8665-e5566c16db9d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"62a901b9603195b5918af3fc02439ce6e935cfe670a9e4410a7d6f30f59075f0","event_uuid":"afa15917-f761-4a4c-a4f2-499a6d252bc8","position":{"commit_sha":"6ac0a05d369cedbfbedf1f75fc9f742ebc8e9c45","position":"1788411455288191001-afa15917-f761-4a4c-a4f2-499a6d252bc8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3acf5631aa4a0caabc6cace53cc7f69efd92ad1f992237182120d5bdc87135f6","event_uuid":"9c93007a-aa18-4ee6-8036-05616636847c","position":{"commit_sha":"2be40e3bd38a13775bcfc5576d8080676144953a","position":"1788412178801943001-9c93007a-aa18-4ee6-8036-05616636847c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-259_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"72e08d92-bab9-41e6-a77e-0524c3443c0b","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## RCA COMPLETE — confirmed root cause, and THE OUTAGE IS STILL ACTIVE\n\nFirst correction to the ticket: it says 'more than 20 minutes'. I verified live just now — `https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp` returns **502 right now, ~4 hours in, with no self-recovery**. Discriminating probe: `/mcp` = 502 while `/review/health` = 200 and `/` = 200, so nginx, Gerrit and the review-bot are all healthy and only the rebar_mcp upstream is dead.\n\n## Confirmed mechanism (on-box, read-only SSM)\n\n1. **The MCP container was OOM-KILLED.** `docker inspect` on `rebar-mcp-8db373933654-8093`: `OOMKilled=true Exit=137 RestartCount=1 Status=exited`, Finished `2026-09-03T01:36:51Z` = **18:36:51 PDT**. The plan-review job started 18:31:33 PDT. **The container died ~3 minutes into the gate run.** Host is a t4g.large, 8 GiB.\n2. **nginx still points at the dead port.** `/etc/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf` contains exactly `server 127.0.0.1:8093;` — the port of that exited container. A single backend, no `max_fails`/`fail_timeout`/`backup`/`proxy_next_upstream`, so one dead port is a total outage. Hence 502 rather than a connection refusal.\n3. **`restart: always` did not save it** — RestartCount=1 and the container is still `exited`.\n\n## Why it persists — recovery is STRUCTURALLY IMPOSSIBLE right now\n\nRedeploy is the only recovery path, and every attempt fails at build:\n\n    error: Required uv version `==0.12.7` does not match the running version `0.12.9`\n\npyproject.toml:346 pins `required-version = \"==0.12.7\"` while the Dockerfiles `COPY --from=ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv:latest`, which has moved to 0.12.9. Autodeploy is looping on this — fail#3 backoff 240s, fail#4 backoff 480s — so MCP can never rebuild. Filed separately as `febd-6b13-1976-43be` (curbable-regardable-lemming), linked, claimed, and being fixed FIRST since it is the prerequisite.\n\n## A hypothesis I had, correctly REFUTED\n\nI suspected `mcp_mem_abort`/`mcp_retire_cap` — the alarms I had just fixed in bff5. Both are **0.0 in every 900s bucket 15:00-21:45 PDT**, and neither has fired since 2026-08-30. They are DEPLOY-PATH markers, not observers of the serving process, so a KERNEL OOM-kill is invisible to them. Recording this because it is the interesting part: the instrumentation that exists for 'MCP ran out of memory' does not observe the case that actually happened.\n\n## The detection gap (AC(b)) is total\n\n`observability.sh:46-58` probes exactly two endpoints and publishes `gerrit_healthy` and `reviewbot_healthy`. There is **no `mcp_healthy` metric** — confirmed by `list-metrics` on namespace rebar/host. The container's own `/health` is not routed by any nginx location, so it is unreachable from outside the box. The deploy declares success at the flip and never re-validates. So nothing in the system can observe that /mcp is 502.\n\n## Latent defect worth its own attention\n\nIn `autodeploy.sh`, `mcp_retire_sweep`'s live-backend guard `[ \"$p\" = \"$live\" ] && continue` sits only inside the `Running=true` branch (~line 714). An exited-but-live container falls through to the else branch and is `docker rm`'d while the nginx include still names its port — which is exactly the state observed here. That converts a transient crash into a permanent 502.\n\n## Also noted\n\nRoot disk is back to **76% (46G/60G)** and climbing — relevant to `3276-2f81-8c75-4ddd` and epic `6202`, since the 60 GiB grow was explicitly an unwedge, not a fix.\n\nPrior art from the search: `d240-824a-dd04-4cdb` (event-loop block, same nginx-alive/upstream-dead signature), `9d40-1db8-1bcc-4f91` (22min of 502 on the sibling /review service; its fix added a per-container healthcheck), `d80d-7be7-1c0a-4231` (added the very `review_plan_start`/`gate_status` surface in use when this broke).","timestamp":1788412178801943001}],"created_at":1788411304995986001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6a7ad30c-7ec9-44b6-9fd0-f9d3a3c457af","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ee0c-1d25-1652-43c3"}],"description":"## Observed\nOn 2026-09-02 the configured rebar MCP endpoint initially accepted tracker calls and started plan-review job 1788399093580353346-ab9badfce4eb4b45a6db70794296455e. A later status poll returned \"Transport closed\"; every subsequent rebar MCP call returned nginx HTTP 502 for more than 20 minutes, including a fresh user-requested retry. The local CLI remained functional.\n\n## Impact\nAgents cannot poll gate results, claim work, or perform tracker operations through the required MCP surface. Long gate state is ambiguous and restarting it risks duplicate billed work.\n\n## Reproduction\n1. Start an async plan review through MCP.\n2. Poll gate_status for its job handle.\n3. Observe transport closure followed by persistent HTTP 502 responses.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- The deployed MCP endpoint remains reachable during and after long async gate jobs.\n- An unhealthy upstream is detected and recovered or reported with an actionable health signal.\n- A regression test or operational probe covers loss of the MCP upstream while a gate job is active.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"9f9a407a-1e5d-4fcf-8665-e5566c16db9d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["bug","mcp","availability","ops"],"ticket_id":"9ea3-7d07-ea55-4496","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Configured rebar MCP endpoint returns persistent HTTP 502 after async gate start","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["97efd87a-2d6b-4333-a55e-5833d9d07cce","6a7ad30c-7ec9-44b6-9fd0-f9d3a3c457af","9f9a407a-1e5d-4fcf-8665-e5566c16db9d","afa15917-f761-4a4c-a4f2-499a6d252bc8","9c93007a-aa18-4ee6-8036-05616636847c"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788416054443269001,"uuid":"cdb043db-ac84-4681-ab48-11ca173932ca"}